ery powerful and i  want to encourage everyone watching to  put questions on facebook and youtube  about really anything regarding  education it could be a single gender  education it could be you know this  question around  public schools charter schools it could  be how we're going to do distance  learning and we'll talk a little bit  more about that uh but david as you've  gone on this journey i guess how many  first of all how many years has it been  and what has been kind of your maybe  some of your things you've been  struggling the most with that you're  still trying to figure out and then what  have been some of the the big wins that  you're like wow that's a powerful data  point that shows that we're on the right  track  well there are a few things uh sal i  would tell you that first of all i've  been in education for over 30 years  myself having been a teacher and  assistant principal founding principal  not only the eagle academy but of a  wonderful co-ed school in the bronx as  well so this is a space that i've  dedicated my life to um there are a  number of things that we have learned in  the space for boys but we've also seen  very broadly really for boys and and for  girls um  internationally there have been some  studies that have been done around boys  and and the biggest thing that emerges  is that boys disconnect from school  because school is boring  the connection to what they're doing in  class to what their real interests are  very often are not aligned  and most teachers will tell you that  they recognize that but they struggle  with how to figure out how to how to  make that connection  um so intuitively they know that boys  check out easily um but you've got to  figure out how do you make your lessons  more fast-paced more engaging um in  order for boys to really stay focused  and they've got to be relevant you've  got to be talking about issues that  really do make a difference and that's  where i think we begin to see the  overlap between